0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"study":{"id":"twitter","title":"The account was real. The request was not.","category":"Social-engineering case","year":"2020","subtitle":"The Twitter account-takeover incident","fictional":false,"difficulty":"Investigation & identity","summary":"Misuse of access to internal tools enabled high-profile accounts to publish a cryptocurrency scam, illustrating the gap between account authenticity and message legitimacy.","story":["In July 2020, prominent Twitter accounts published messages promoting a cryptocurrency payment scheme. The posts appeared on genuine accounts, making ordinary “check the profile” advice inadequate.","Public authorities described social engineering and misuse of internal access in the investigation and charges. The case shows why employee identity, privileged tools, approval paths, and audit logs are central to platform security.","For evidence handling, preserve the account posts, backend audit records, access approvals, and payment trail through lawful process. A verified badge or authentic account can establish where a message appeared, but not that the legitimate owner intended the request."],"timeline":[{"date":"15 July 2020","event":"High-profile accounts publish scam messages."},{"date":"July 2020","event":"Platform containment and investigation proceed."},{"date":"31 July 2020","event":"US authorities announce charges concerning the incident."}],"issue":"How social engineering and privileged access can undermine trust in authentic accounts.","holding":"Investigative lesson: examine internal access and account-control records, not merely the public profile. The cited charges are allegations and procedural history, not a substitute for reviewing the final case outcome.","lessons":["A genuine account can be compromised.","Protect and monitor privileged internal tools.","Preserve access and approval logs.","Separate platform provenance from human intent.","Use precise language for charges, allegations, and findings."],"questions":["What internal records would you request?","How would you explain account authenticity to a non-technical reader?","Which controls reduce the impact of a successful social-engineering attempt?"],"sources":["twitter"],"topics":["3.4","3.12","5.3"]}}],[["$","script","script-0",{"src":"/_next/static/chunks/07qngb6s2_y2q.js","async":true}]],["$","$L3",null,{"children":["$","$4",null,{"name":"Next.MetadataOutlet","children":"$@5"}]}]]}],"isPartial":false,"staleTime":300,"varyParams":null,"buildId":"mMiCr23A_-Cpk0hZkfT7X"}
